# Shadowing: when two instances for the same class+type exist at
# different scope levels, evidence-passing finds the innermost first.
# Here both instances are for Integer but produce different results.
# A helper function dispatches 'show' — its effect chain carries
# the call site's scope where the later instance appears after the
# earlier one. The scan finds the later (innermost) instance first.
[
  Showable: [class [let a]
    show: []]
  [instance Showable
    [let a@Integer]: [show: [fn [let x] "first"]]]
  [instance Showable
    [let a@Integer]: [show: [fn [let x] "second"]]]

  # Direct dispatch — innermost (later) instance should win
  result: [show 42]
]
=== out
["Showable": []  "ɪɴꜱᴛᴀɴᴄᴇ⧼Showable∷show⟨Integer⟩⧽": [fn [let x] ...]  "result": "second"]
